/**
@mainpage Nane

<strong>A modern C++23 scientific computing library.</strong>

Nane provides small and composable tools for numerical computing while
using Eigen directly for vectors and matrices.

## Example

Consider the initial value problem

@f[
\dot{x}(t) = -t^2x(t),
\qquad
x(0) = 5.3.
@f]

It can be solved with Heun's method:

@code{.cpp}
#include <nane/geometry/uniform_grid.hpp>
#include <nane/numerics/ode/one_step.hpp>

int main()
{
    nane::uniform_grid<1> time_grid({
        {0.0, 2.0, 101},
    });

    auto derivative = [](double t, double x)
    {
        return -t * t * x;
    };

    auto solution = nane::heun(derivative, 5.3, time_grid);

    return 0;
}
@endcode

## Design

Nane uses Eigen directly for vector and matrix representations and does not
introduce another linear algebra abstraction on top of Eigen.

Numerical algorithms are provided as small, composable free functions.

*/
